  "explanation": "The replacement preserves every meaningful inherited behavior while removing fixed-time timing assertions and a helper that polled in 50 ms intervals. Captured and noncaptured synchronization-context behavior is proven through explicit barriers and a single deterministic pump operation. The greenfield cohort additionally covers the complete public TaskUtil capability boundary: cached tasks, exact fault and cancellation state, completion-source creation, cancellation registration, idempotent completion, argument validation, and the absence of desktop Windows framework references from the product assembly. Timeouts are safety boundaries only and are never used as behavior oracles."
